From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:35:03 -0600
Subject: build-web: add --no-threads for single-threaded WASM builds

`build-web` always builds multi-threaded WASM: it forces the nightly
toolchain, passes `-Z build-std=std,panic_abort` and sets atomics /
shared-memory rustflags. The output needs cross-origin isolation
(COOP/COEP), which many hosts cannot provide. The docs already describe
a main-thread-only mode (`default_dart_async: false`), but the CLI gives
no way to build for it and the crate does not compile without the
`thread-pool` feature on wasm: the generated web default handler uses a
thread-local pool that has no `BaseThreadPool` implementation there.

- build-web: add `--threads` (default true). With `--no-threads` it
  skips `-Z build-std`, leaves RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN unset unless
  `--wasm-pack-rustup-toolchain` is given, and passes only a
  user-supplied `--wasm-pack-rustflags`. Stable Rust is enough.
  `WasmPackRustflagsResolution.rustflags` becomes nullable to express
  "leave cargo's own configuration alone".
- frb_rust: implement `BaseThreadPool` for the thread-local pool the
  generated web default handler uses, so the crate compiles with
  `thread-pool` disabled.
- frb_rust: without `thread-pool`, `Handler::wrap_normal` is a
  compile-time error naming the fix (`#[frb(sync)]`, `async fn` or
  `default_dart_async: false`) instead of failing at link/run time.
- docs: describe the three steps in the cross-origin page.

Default behavior (threads on) is unchanged.

`entrypoint.g.dart` is produced by `build_cli`, which frb_dart's
pubspec comments out (kevmoo/build_cli#168). The added block follows the
generator's formatting for long flags; it needs regenerating once
`build_cli` is re-enabled.

Checks run on 1e4df906 (master after v2.14.0-beta.2; fork branch
web-build-no-threads @ 315e93a2), Dart 3.13.7, rustc/cargo 1.99.0,
wasm-pack 0.15.1, wasm-bindgen 0.2.128:
- `dart analyze lib/src/cli test/build_web_executor_test.dart
  test/entrypoint_test.dart test/build_web_entrypoint_test.dart` in
  frb_dart: no issues.
- `dart test` on those three test files: 24 passed, including the new
  rustflags resolution test with `threads: false` and
  `executeBuildWeb(threads: false)` asserting no `-Z`/`build-std` in the
  wasm-pack argv and no RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN or
  CARGO_TARGET_WASM32_UNKNOWN_UNKNOWN_RUSTFLAGS in its env.
- `cargo test -p flutter_rust_bridge --lib`: 98 passed with default
  features, and 98 passed with `--no-default-features --features
  anyhow,dart-opaque,log,portable-atomic,rust-async,user-utils,wasm-start`
  (includes the new
  thread_pool::stub::tests::web_default_handler_pool_type_is_a_thread_pool).
- `cargo check -p flutter_rust_bridge --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`
  with those features: finished, with the same 5 warnings as the base.
- A scratch crate calling `frb_generated_default_handler!()` with
  `thread-pool` disabled: at the base, 6 x E0277 (`&LocalKey<
  SimpleThreadPool>: BaseThreadPool` not satisfied), plus E0599
  (`wrap_normal`) with a plain function; with this change it builds, and
  a plain (non-sync, non-async) function fails with E0080 naming the
  fix.
- `dart run bin/flutter_rust_bridge.dart build-web -c <crate> -o web
  --release --no-threads --verbose` on a minimal wasm-bindgen cdylib ran
  `wasm-pack build -t no-modules ...` on stable rustc 1.99.0 with only
  RUSTFLAGS/CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS removed from the env and produced
  the .js + _bg.wasm pair. The default (threads) invocation on the same
  crate is byte-identical to the base: `-Z build-std=std,panic_abort`,
  RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=nightly and the ten shared-memory rustflags.

Rebase notes: moved from 1e4df906 to v2.13.0, the latest stable
release, whose build-web is older. Ported to it: the env keeps
v2.13.0's RUSTFLAGS (not CARGO_TARGET_WASM32_UNKNOWN_UNKNOWN_RUSTFLAGS)
and sets it only when there are rustflags to pass; v2.13.0 inherits the
parent environment and has no removedParentEnvKeys, so a RUSTFLAGS set
by the user still reaches cargo with --no-threads. The context lines
naming `--skip-tool-install` and the Dart Wasm entrypoint are gone
(neither exists at v2.13.0). Tests: the `executeBuildWeb(threads:
false)` argv/env test is dropped, because v2.13.0 has no runCommandImpl
seam to record the wasm-pack call; the parser test is reduced to
`parseConfig` (default true, `--no-threads` false), because
parseBuildWebConfigToArgs is private there. The Rust and docs hunks
are unchanged.

Checked on v2.13.0 with this series (together with the Web Worker
change after it), Flutter 3.47.9, Chrome 158.0.8127.36: the p0g web
runtime proof (`bash tool/web_runtime_proof/run.sh frb`, from a clean
pub/Cargo fixture without FRB overrides) built the patched codegen, ran
`build-web --no-threads --release` to a wasm module, and a dedicated
classic Web Worker without cross-origin isolation returned
`"value":"rust:5050","hasDocument":false,"isolated":false,"errors":[]`.
The other checks above have not been rerun on v2.13.0.

